WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.622
This tutorial builds a set of blocks called Title every clip.

2
00:00:04.622 --> 00:00:10.164
It adds a styled title at the playhead, and then fades in every clip in your edit.

3
00:00:10.164 --> 00:00:17.530
You build it without writing code, check it with a preview, and apply it as a single step that can be undone.

4
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.963
Open the Blocks panel from the tool dock.

5
00:00:20.963 --> 00:00:23.188
The block studio fills the screen.

6
00:00:23.188 --> 00:00:29.471
The palette is on the left, the canvas is in the middle, and the run controls are in the header.

7
00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:35.230
If blocks are new to you, the Tutorial button in the header offers a guided walkthrough.

8
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:41.887
Every set of blocks begins with the green block named When Apply is pressed.

9
00:00:41.887 --> 00:00:46.473
Its Work on setting decides which clips the set applies to.

10
00:00:46.473 --> 00:00:50.749
Choose Every clip, so the blocks act on the whole edit.

11
00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:55.490
Then click the name in the header and enter Title every clip.

12
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.562
Beneath the green block, an Add title block is already connected.

13
00:01:01.562 --> 00:01:09.751
The dot at the bottom of one block joins the dot at the top of the next, so the blocks run in order.

14
00:01:09.751 --> 00:01:13.190
Type Made with blocks into its Text field.

15
00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:20.575
Open the Animate category and drag a Fade in slowly block onto the canvas.

16
00:01:20.575 --> 00:01:27.749
Its Clip field reads clip ID, which means the clip being handled at that moment.

17
00:01:27.749 --> 00:01:32.770
The block will not run yet, because nothing connects it.

18
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:39.455
Open the Flow category and drag a For each clip block onto the canvas.

19
00:01:39.455 --> 00:01:48.104
Connect it beneath the title block, then join its repeat dot on the right to the Fade in slowly block.

20
00:01:48.104 --> 00:01:53.870
Set its filter to all, so the fade runs once for every kind of clip.

21
00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.989
Select Preview in the header.

22
00:01:56.989 --> 00:02:04.753
It lists exactly what Apply would change, one line per change, and it does not touch your edit.

23
00:02:04.753 --> 00:02:08.594
When the list is correct, select Apply to edit.

24
00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:15.050
The title lands at the playhead, and every clip fades in, as one undoable step.

25
00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:22.636
Your blocks save to your account as you work, and they appear in the Tools panel of the Studio.

26
00:02:22.636 --> 00:02:32.710
The Share button copies a short code that anyone can paste into their own Tools panel, and the Code tab shows the same blocks as JavaScript.

27
00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.189
That completes the block coding tutorial.

28
00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:44.243
The same blocks run through the same operations and validation as the API, so an agent could send exactly what you built.

29
00:02:44.243 --> 00:02:48.170
The next tutorial turns a single clip into a finished edit.

